<div class="page-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">VISUALIZER GUIDE</span><h1>See your ideas take shape.</h1><p>A photo editor for exploring floor and wall finishes.</p></div><a class="button" href="<?= $u('visualizer') ?>">Open visualizer ↗</a></div><section class="panel php-help"><h2>Start with a room</h2><p>Choose Luxury Living or Sunlit Living for prepared SAM 2 floor and wall selections. Other rooms start with manual selections. Choose a sample texture, select Floor or Feature wall, and turn on Apply material.</p><h2>Use your own room photo</h2><ol><li>Use Choose room photo at the top of the visualizer to select a JPEG, PNG or WebP under 12 MB.</li><li>Select Perspective corners. Drag the four points to follow the floor or wall.</li><li>Reset selection to corners, then use Erase selection to remove furniture and Restore selection to recover missing areas.</li><li>Adjust pattern repeats, rotation, grout and shading. Use Show original to compare.</li><li>Save photo design to this browser, or Download image to keep a PNG copy.</li></ol><h2>Use your original marble photo</h2><p>Select Floor or Feature wall, then use Or use your original marble photo to choose a clear, straight-on image of the stone. The editor shows progress while it prepares and places the image. Your marble photo stays on this device and is included in saved designs. Choose a sample swatch to switch back. Surface corners and furniture exclusions still need your review.</p><h2>Prepare an AI selection</h2><p>Automatic SAM 2 inference is a separate local Python step. Include/exclude points in the editor do not run a model. Download the source photo and selection prompts, process them with the project’s local SAM runner, then import its JSON file using Prepared SAM selection. Ask your operator to prepare the selection file with the local SAM 2 runner, then import it here to continue editing.</p><h2>If the editor does not start</h2><p>Enable JavaScript and graphics acceleration/WebGL in your browser. Open the site through localhost or HTTPS, rather than opening a file directly. If browser storage is disabled or full, export the image instead of relying on saved designs.</p><h2>What the preview means</h2><p>Photos stay on this device. Saved designs are separated for guests and signed-in accounts in this browser; they do not sync to another device. Clearing browser data removes them. Samples are visual references, not stock or prices. The preview does not measure your room, reconstruct 3D, or guarantee exact colour or scale.</p></section>
